{
  "title": "Dua for safety from illness and ailments",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "Imam Ali (a) said: put your hand on the ailing part and repeat the following three times:\nاَللهُ اَللهُ اَللهُ رَبِّىْ حَقًّا لَّا اُشْرِكُ بِهِ شَيْئًا\nALLAAHO ALLAAHO ALLAAHO RABBEE HAQQAL LAA USHRIKU BIHI SHAY-AA\nAllah, Allah, Allah is truly my Lord; I associate nothing with Him.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَنْتَ لَهَا وَ لِكُلِّ عَظِيْمَةٍ فَفَرِّجْهَا عَنِّىْ\nALLAAHUMMA ANTA LAHAA WA LI-KULLI A'ZEEMATIN FA-FARRIJHAA A'NNEE\nO Allah, You are sufficient for it and for every great calamity; so relieve it from me.\nImam al-Sadiq (a) said in this regard: put your hand on the ailing part and say:\nبِسْمِ اللهِ\nBISMIL LAAH\nIn the name of Allah,\nThen rub the ailing part with your hand and repeat the following evil-repelling prayer (ta'widh) seven times:\nاَعُوْذُ بِعِزَّةِ اللّٰهِ وَ اَعُوْذُ بِقُدْرَةِ اللّٰهِ وَ اَعُوْذُ بِجَلَالِ اللّٰهِ وَ اَعُوْذُ بِعَظَمَةِ اللّٰهِ وَ اَعُوْذُ بِجَمْعِ اللّٰهِ وَ اَعُوْذُ بِرَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَ اٰلِهٖ وَ اَعُوْذُ بِاَسْمَاۤءِ اللّٰهِ مِنْ شَرِّ مَا اَحْذَرُ وَ مِنْ شَرِّ مَا اَخَافُ عَلٰى نَفْسِىْ\nA'OOZU BI-I'ZZATIL LAAHI WA A'OOZU BI-QUDRATIL LAAHI WA A'OOZU BI-JALAALIL LAAHI WA A'OOZU BI-A'ZAMATIL LAAHI WA A'OOZU BI-JAM-I'L LAAHI WA A'OOZU BI-RASOOLIL LAAHI SALLAL LAAHO A'LAYHI WA AALIHI WA A'OOZU BI-ASMAAA-IL LAAHI MIN SHARRI MAA AHZARU WA MIN SHARRI MAA AKHAAFU A'LAA NAFSEE\nI seek refuge in the might of Allah, and I seek refuge in the power of Allah, and I seek refuge in the majesty of Allah, and I seek refuge in the greatness of Allah, and I seek refuge in the totality of Allah, and I seek refuge in the Messenger of Allah — Allah's blessings be upon him and his Household — and I seek refuge in the names of Allah from the evil of what I am wary of and from the evil of what I fear for myself."
}
